@.str.6 = private unnamed_addr constant [2315 x i8] c"\0AA LineSet contains points and lines joining them and optionally attributes on\0Athe points and lines.  The ``LineSet`` class stores the attribute data in\0Akey-value maps, where the key is the attribute name and value is a Tensor\0Acontaining the attribute data.  There are two maps: one each for ``point``\0Aand ``line``.\0A\0AThe attributes of the line set have different levels::\0A\0A    import open3d as o3d\0A\0A    dtype_f = o3d.core.float32\0A    dtype_i = o3d.core.int32\0A\0A    # Create an empty line set\0A    # Use lineset.point to access the point attributes\0A    # Use lineset.line to access the line attributes\0A    lineset = o3d.t.geometry.LineSet()\0A\0A    # Default attribute: point.positions, line.indices\0A    # These attributes is created by default and are required by all line\0A    # sets. The shape must be (N, 3) and (N, 2) respectively. The device of\0A    # \22positions\22 determines the device of the line set.\0A    lineset.point.positions = o3d.core.Tensor([[0, 0, 0],\0A                                                  [0, 0, 1],\0A                                                  [0, 1, 0],\0A                                                  [0, 1, 1]], dtype_f, device)\0A    lineset.line.indices = o3d.core.Tensor([[0, 1],\0A                                               [1, 2],\0A                                               [2, 3],\0A                                               [3, 0]], dtype_i, device)\0A\0A    # Common attributes: line.colors\0A    # Common attributes are used in built-in line set operations. The\0A    # spellings must be correct. For example, if \22color\22 is used instead of\0A    # \22color\22, some internal operations that expects \22colors\22 will not work.\0A    # \22colors\22 must have shape (N, 3) and must be on the same device as the\0A    # line set.\0A    lineset.line.colors = o3d.core.Tensor([[0.0, 0.0, 0.0],\0A                                              [0.1, 0.1, 0.1],\0A                                              [0.2, 0.2, 0.2],\0A                                              [0.3, 0.3, 0.3]], dtype_f, device)\0A\0A    # User-defined attributes\0A    # You can also attach custom attributes. The value tensor must be on the\0A    # same device as the line set. The are no restrictions on the shape or\0A    # dtype, e.g.,\0A    lineset.point.labels = o3d.core.Tensor(...)\0A    lineset.line.features = o3d.core.Tensor(...)\0A\00", align 1
